WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.840
This is the Singularity Daily, for Monday, November 16.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.010
Here's your day in superintelligence, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.470
It's test week. Nvidia reports Tuesday. Thursday,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:22.140
Anthropic goes public, and Korea sits its big exam.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.850
And Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent wants an outsider running Nvidia.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.690
Now, the bets.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.790
Anthropic's early backers are about to see what their bets are worth.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.230
A fund Ashton Kutcher co-founded put in $435 million.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.300
Its stake could be worth about $7 billion.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.300
And a British trader's $10 million bet could be worth up to $3.5 billion.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:53.600
Meanwhile,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:59.000
China's Meituan released a giant open AI model trained without a single Nvidia chip.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.350
Speaking of exams. In Korea,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.970
the tax exam's top scorer missed one of 160 questions.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.040
He confessed on Sunday: a hidden camera,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.710
an AI tool, and the answers on his phone.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.100
He said the top score "was not the result of

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.200
fair effort." Police are now investigating.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.420
And with Korea's college entrance exam on Thursday,

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.390
the president's office called an emergency meeting.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.390
This week in Nature,

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:35.830
Berkeley researchers trained an AI on over 440,000 heart scans.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.280
It flagged people at risk of sudden cardi

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.600
ac death that standard checks would miss.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.640
The catch?

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:51.010
Anthropic's own filing warns its models could take harmful actions nobody directed.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.980
It even warns of "existential risks to humanity." In a stock offering.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.230
Back to the machines.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:07.690
Hong Kong's airport is the first to repaint its runways with robots.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:14.190
A centre line took three hours. Now it's one, and people still paint the curves.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.920
And Penn engineers made soft robot muscles.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.560
A robot hand used them to play piano.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:28.640
That's test week. AI can ace the test. Passing it honestly is still on us.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.540
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
